To prevent routes from being reflected back to the originating peers in a BGP route reflection cluster, enable the `split-horizon` feature in your BGP group configuration:

```cli
configure router bgp
    group "CLUSTER_GROUP_NAME"
        split-horizon
    exit
exit
```

**Key points:**  
1. **`split-horizon`** ensures routes learned from a peer in the group are never reflected back to any peer in the same group.  
2. Apply this to the BGP group containing your route reflection clients.  
3. This operates per-address-family and works for all peer types (iBGP/eBGP).  

Replace `CLUSTER_GROUP_NAME` with your actual BGP group name. No restart is needed—changes apply to new updates immediately.
