## Proposed answer:
To configure BGP to ignore the IGP cost to the next-hop in the best path selection process, use the following command:

```cli
configure router bgp best-path-selection ignore-nh-metric
```

This command disables the comparison of the resolved distance to the BGP next-hop during route selection. The decision process will now rely solely on standard BGP tiebreakers (e.g., AS path length, origin type, MED, etc.) for paths with identical NLRI.
