To adjust the BGP path selection for labeled IPv6 routes so that external and internal neighbors are treated equally, use the following command:

```cli
configure router bgp best-path-selection ebgp-ibgp-equal label-ipv6
```

This configuration ensures the BGP decision process ignores the EBGP vs. IBGP distinction when selecting the best path for labeled IPv6 routes. Routes from internal peers with better metrics (e.g., lower MED) will now be preferred over external peers if they meet other path selection criteria.
