## User question:
On a Nokia 7750 SR, what's the way to set up a longer stale route timer (like 3600s) locally, even if a neighbor is pushing a different value in their link capacity info? I want our box to ignore what the peer is advertising and stick to the 1-hour timeout we need.
---
## Proposed answer:
To set a longer stale route timer of 3600 seconds and ignore the peer's advertised value, use the `helper-override-stale-time` command within the BGP long-lived graceful restart configuration:

```
configure router bgp
    graceful-restart
        long-lived
            helper-override-stale-time 3600
```

This configuration forces the router to use the locally configured 1-hour timeout for stale routes, overriding any value received from the neighbor.
