- `send-to-ebgp ipv4`: Advertises the link-bandwidth extended community to EBGP peers for IPv4 routes.  
- `add-to-received-ebgp ipv4`: Adds link-bandwidth metadata to IPv4 routes received from directly connected EBGP peers.  
- `aggregate-used-paths ipv4`: Aggregates bandwidth values from multipaths when re-advertising routes with `next-hop-self`.  

Replace `<group_name>` with your BGP group name. Adjust the `ipv4` address family if working with other families (e.g., `vpn-ipv4` for labeled routes).
