To adjust the trust level (preference) for labeled BGP routes to 150 and prioritize other paths first, use the following CLI command:

```bash
configure router bgp label-preference 150
```

**Explanation:**  
- This command sets the preference for labeled BGP routes to `150` (lower values are more trusted).  
- Labeled routes (150) will be **less preferred** than the default non-labeled BGP routes (default preference 170), ensuring other paths are prioritized.  
- Labeled routes will only be used if no other paths (with lower preference values) are available.  

Apply this globally under `bgp` to affect all labeled BGP routes.
